---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import Giscus from '../../components/Giscus.astro';

const lang = 'en' as const;
---

<Layout
  title="Images, Sizing & Image Hosting — Attachment Folders, Width Presets, Typora Templates & S3/GitHub Upload"
  description="How SoloMD saves, resizes, and uploads images: _assets and per-note folders, Typora path templates, pasted image default width presets, right-click scaling, PicGo/S3/GitHub hosting, and anti-hotlink rendering."
  lang={lang}
>
  <Header lang={lang} />
  <main id="main">
    <article class="container docs-article">
      <nav class="breadcrumbs">
        <a href="/">Home</a> / <a href="/docs/">Docs</a> / <span>Images &amp; Attachments</span>
      </nav>

      <h1>Images, Sizing &amp; Image Hosting</h1>
      <p class="lead">Where pasted screenshots land, how to control their display size, and how to upload to an image host.</p>

      <h2>1. What happens when you paste</h2>
      <p>
        Copy a screenshot to the clipboard, place the caret in a note, and press <kbd>Ctrl/⌘ + V</kbd> (or drag an image file into the window) — SoloMD writes the image next to your note and inserts a relative Markdown link (automatically encoding spaces and normalizing Windows backslashes):
      </p>
      <pre><code>my-folder/
├── note.md          ← you pasted here
└── _assets/
    └── image-20261102-093012.png</code></pre>

      <h2>2. Three attachment folder modes</h2>
      <p>Open <strong>Settings → Writing</strong> and choose <em>“Where to save pasted/dropped images”</em>:</p>
      <table class="kb-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Mode</th><th>Images go to</th><th>Best for</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <th>Shared (default)</th>
            <td>One folder per directory — <code>_assets/</code> by default, or rename it to <code>images</code> (or any name) in the field below.</td>
            <td>Simple vaults; <code>_assets</code> is hidden in the file tree by default to reduce clutter.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th>Per-file</th>
            <td><code>&lt;note&gt;.assets/</code> next to each note (e.g. <code>foo.md</code> gets <code>foo.assets/</code>).</td>
            <td>Keeping each note self-contained; renaming <code>foo.md</code> in the file tree renames <code>foo.assets/</code> and rewrites links automatically.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th>Custom (Typora-style)</th>
            <td>A path template supporting <code>$&#123;filename&#125;</code>, such as <code>./images/$&#123;filename&#125;/</code> or <code>../attachments/</code>.</td>
            <td>Vaults migrated from Typora.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2>3. Default pasted image width &amp; right-click resizing</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Default width preset</strong>: in <strong>Settings → Writing → Default pasted image width</strong>, set a default scale (e.g. <code>50%</code>, <code>67%</code>, <code>80%</code>, or a pixel width) so high-DPI screenshots don’t overwhelm the page.</li>
        <li><strong>Right-click resize &amp; Copy Image</strong>: right-click any image in the editor to resize it on the spot (25% / 50% / 67% / 80% / 100%) or copy the bitmap back to the system clipboard.</li>
        <li><strong>Side-by-side inline images</strong>: multiple inline <code>&lt;img&gt;</code> tags on the same line stay side by side in both Live Edit and Preview.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Image hosting (PicGo / SM.MS / S3 / R2 / GitHub)</h2>
      <p>
        Configure <strong>Settings → Image Upload</strong> to upload images to <strong>PicGo</strong>, <strong>SM.MS</strong>, <strong>S3-compatible object storage (AWS S3, Cloudflare R2, MinIO, OSS, COS)</strong>, or a <strong>GitHub repository</strong>. You can upload automatically on paste or batch-upload local images in the current note from the command palette.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Anti-hotlink external images &amp; Android SAF support</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Anti-hotlink <code>no-referrer</code></strong>: SoloMD sets <code>referrerpolicy="no-referrer"</code> before loading external images and decodes HTML-escaped <code>&amp;amp;</code> query strings, so Gitee, signed cloud URLs, and anti-hotlink image hosts render cleanly across Live Edit and Preview.</li>
        <li><strong>Android &amp; iOS</strong>: pick photos from the system picker on Android SAF vaults and resolve relative paths (<code>./pic/foo.png</code>, <code>../assets/bar.jpg</code>) seamlessly in Live Edit, Preview, and PDF/DOCX exports.</li>
      </ul>

      <Giscus />
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer lang={lang} />
</Layout>
